.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt GETENT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm getent
.Nd get entries from administrative databases
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl i
.Op Fl s Ar service
.Ar database
.Op Ar key ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the entries that match each
.Ar key
in
.Ar database ,
or every entry of
.Ar database
when no key is given.
It asks the C library, so it sees exactly what programs see.
musl has no name service switch: users, groups and shadow entries come
from the files in
.Pa /etc ,
hosts from
.Pa /etc/hosts
and DNS, services from
.Pa /etc/services ,
and protocols from the table built into musl.
.Pp
The output formats and exit statuses match the
.Nm
of glibc, so scripts written for it keep working.
.Pp
The databases are:
.Bl -tag -width initgroups
.It Cm passwd
Users, by name or numeric user ID.
.It Cm group
Groups, by name or numeric group ID.
.It Cm shadow
Shadow password entries, by user name.
Only root can read them.
.It Cm initgroups
The group IDs a user belongs to, including the primary group.
A key is required.
.It Cm hosts
Addresses of a host name, IPv6 first and then IPv4, or the name of an
address.
Without a key, the entries of
.Pa /etc/hosts .
.It Cm ahosts , ahostsv4 , ahostsv6
The results of
.Xr getaddrinfo 3
for a host name, one line per address and socket type, for any address
family, IPv4 only, or IPv6 with IPv4-mapped addresses.
.It Cm services
Network services, by name or port number, optionally followed by
.No / Ns Ar protocol ,
for example
.Ql ssh
or
.Ql 53/udp .
.It Cm protocols
IP protocols, by name or number.
.El
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i , Fl -no-idn
Accepted for compatibility with glibc and ignored.
.It Fl s Ar service , Fl -service Ns = Ns Ar service
Accepted for compatibility with glibc and ignored, since musl has
only one source for each database.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a usage message and the list of databases.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Pp
Options may also follow
.Ar database
or a
.Ar key ,
as with glibc.
An argument of
.Fl -
ends the options, so every argument after it is a key.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Every key was found, or the database was listed.
.It 1
An argument is missing, or the database or an option is unknown.
.It 2
At least one key was not found.
.It 3
The database cannot be listed without a key.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check whether a user exists:
.Dl getent passwd unbound >/dev/null || echo "no unbound user"
.Pp
Resolve a name the way programs do:
.Dl getent hosts example.com
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 ,
.Xr getgrnam 3 ,
.Xr getpwnam 3 ,
.Xr getservbyname 3 ,
.Xr getspnam 3 ,
.Xr group 5 ,
.Xr hosts 5 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr services 5
